From: Bartlomiej Dudzik <15948633+BobrImperator@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not select Bevy's `x11` feature

The `[dependencies.bevy]` feature list enabled `x11`, which pulls the X11
windowing backend (`x11rb`, `x11-dl`) into every application that depends
on Hanabi, including Wayland-only ones that never select it. The windowing
backend is the application's choice: Hanabi renders through `bevy_render`
and needs no particular window system.

Drop `x11` and keep the rest of the list. The GPU tests and examples still
open windows through the dev-dependency on Bevy with default features.
---
 Cargo.toml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 85f7140..88df111 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -80,7 +80,6 @@ features = [
   "bevy_render",
   "bevy_asset",
   "bevy_log",
-  "x11",
 ]
 
 [package.metadata.docs.rs]
